@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy — RatPDF";
    ViewData["Description"] = "How RatPDF handles uploaded files, account data, cookies, and third-party services. Files are processed on secure servers and deleted after conversion.";
}
<head>
    <meta name="robots" content="index, follow">
</head>

<article class="container my-5">
    <div class="card border-0 shadow-sm p-4 p-md-5" style="border-radius: 16px;">
        <h1 class="fw-bold mb-3">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="text-muted">Last updated: June 2025</p>
        <p>
            RatPDF ("we", "our", "the service") operates ratpdf.com and related subdomains.
            This policy explains what information we collect, how uploaded files are handled,
            and your choices.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h4 fw-semibold mt-4">1. Files you upload</h2>
        <p>
            When you use PDF conversion, compression, merge, or similar server-side tools,
            your file is transmitted over <strong>HTTPS</strong> to our application servers
            (hosted on Microsoft Azure).
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>Files are written to temporary server storage only for the duration of processing.</li>
            <li>Completed outputs may be stored in private Azure Blob Storage until you download them or they expire.</li>
            <li>Automated cleanup jobs remove old blobs and job metadata on a schedule.</li>
            <li>We do not manually review document contents except when required to investigate abuse or technical failures you report.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
            Some lightweight utilities (formatters, counters, client-side previews) may process data entirely
            in your browser without uploading the file. Each tool page describes its behaviour.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h4 fw-semibold mt-4">2. Account &amp; billing information</h2>
        <p>If you create an account or subscribe to Pro:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>We store your email address and authentication identifiers.</li>
            <li>Payments are processed by <strong>Razorpay</strong>; we do not store full card numbers on our servers.</li>
            <li>Subscription status and invoice references are kept for billing support and tax records.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="h4 fw-semibold mt-4">3. Technical logs</h2>
        <p>Like most websites, we collect limited technical data:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>IP address, browser type, and referring URL (standard web server logs)</li>
            <li>Anonymous usage counters (tool name, success/failure, file size bucket) to monitor capacity</li>
            <li>Error traces without document content when a conversion fails</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Logs are retained for a short period for security and debugging, then rotated.</p>

        <h2 class="h4 fw-semibold mt-4">4. Cookies &amp; advertising</h2>
        <p>We use cookies for:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Session authentication (signed-in users)</li>
            <li>Remembering daily free-tier usage limits</li>
            <li>Analytics and advertising partners such as <strong>Google AdSense</strong></li>
        </ul>
        <p>
            Third-party ad networks may set their own cookies to serve and measure ads.
            You can control cookies through your browser settings and, where offered,
            <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Google Ads Settings</a>.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h4 fw-semibold mt-4">5. Data sharing</h2>
        <p>We do <strong>not</strong> sell personal information. We share data only with:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Infrastructure providers (Microsoft Azure) under data-processing agreements</li>
            <li>Payment processor (Razorpay) to complete transactions you initiate</li>
            <li>Law enforcement when legally compelled and narrowly scoped</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="h4 fw-semibold mt-4">6. Security measures</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>TLS encryption in transit</li>
            <li>Private blob containers (no public listing of uploads)</li>
            <li>Least-privilege access to production systems</li>
            <li>Regular dependency updates for conversion engines</li>
        </ul>
        <p>No online service can guarantee absolute security; avoid uploading highly classified material.</p>

        <h2 class="h4 fw-semibold mt-4">7. Your rights (GDPR / CCPA)</h2>
        <p>Depending on your location you may request access, correction, or deletion of personal data we hold
        (account email, billing records). Contact us via the <a href="/Home/Contact">contact page</a>.
        Because uploaded PDFs are ephemeral, deletion usually occurs automatically within hours.</p>

        <h2 class="h4 fw-semibold mt-4">8. Children's privacy</h2>
        <p>The service is not directed at children under 13. We do not knowingly collect data from minors.</p>

        <h2 class="h4 fw-semibold mt-4">9. Changes</h2>
        <p>We may update this policy when we add tools or change hosting practices. Material changes will be posted on this page.</p>

        <h2 class="h4 fw-semibold mt-4">10. Contact</h2>
        <p>Questions about privacy: <a href="/Home/Contact">Contact RatPDF</a>.</p>
    </div>
</article>
